      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Pretreatment (i.c.v.) of mice with L-arginine but not D-arginine potentiated beta-endorphin-induced (i.c.v. administered) inhibition of the tail-flick response. The potentiation was attenuated by N omega-nitro-L-arginine methyl ester, a selective inhibitor of nitric oxide synthase. This observation suggests that increased production of nitric oxide from L-arginine mediates the potentiation of beta-endorphin-induced antinociception."},
